            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "marybcurlyq"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Really good salsa; nice and fresh. EASY to make. I put everything in the food processor and it was done in a couple of minutes. I did use 2 jalepenos and that was a bit much. You may just want to use 1 of those!!"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Steven martin"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I followed the recipe exactly. I let it sit overnight and the next morning I took about a third out and put in food processor. I put the puree back with the rest of it and mixed it. Perfect blend of juice and chunks. I took it to our church Picnic and it won first place out of 8 salsa's. The judges ate most of it. Thank you for sharing.",
            "datePublished": "2014-06-13T10:44:16.080Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Nibs1"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Awesome recipe, nice &amp; easy. Only thing I changed was I used a clove of garlic minced and added half cup of fresh corn.",
            "datePublished": "2012-08-11T10:19:12.910Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Chad_"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Very easy to make and I have made this recipe several times, but I do have a couple of comments to make with respect to a handful of other reviews. I do use my food processor for the tomatoes, but I highly recommend not using it for the onion or jalepenos. It's nice to have a bit of substance to your salsa rather than all liquid. I have made this salsa with and without cilantro depending if I had it or not and it is much, much better with the cilantro. It is not an ingredient that should be left out. In my view and those of most others who have tried the salsa I've made, two medium sized fresh jalepenos are either not enough or just right. I've doubled it before and it gets to the point of just barely breaking a forehead sweat while eating it, which is what I like my spicy foods to do.",
            "datePublished": "2011-01-23T13:11:50.220Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Jessica Gillespy Hughson"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Read all the previous reviews before I made this and followed the advice of many to add garlic. A note to those who commented that 4 jalapenos was too spicy, read carefully and you will notice that the recipe calls for 4 TEASPOONS, not 4 whole peppers. Big difference, especially if you are serving anyone who can't stand the heat, LOL.",
            "datePublished": "2013-07-10T09:36:54.850Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "NC Ken"
            },
            "reviewBody": "EXCELLENT! Recommend reducing tomato liquid by removing seeds, then salting them, let stand for half hour to remove excess moisture, then resume recipe. Even better next day!",
            "datePublished": "2023-07-03T08:17:01.867Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Sara Dunn"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This salsa is DELICIOUS! I added 2 whole jalapeños, 4 garlic cloves, the juice of a whole lime and some more salt, then blended it up in my Ninja Bullet. It is so flavorful and fresh. I will definitely be making this again!",
            "datePublished": "2020-08-07T02:19:33.400Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Ceridwen"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Excellent! My go-to salsa recipe. I use the juice and zest of a whole lime and omit the jalapeño seeds.",
            "datePublished": "2013-04-06T11:14:04.850Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "David V W"
            },
            "reviewBody": "So, the base was just fair, and I would have rated it a 3*. I made it twice and the first time, as others have pointed out, was a bit bland. The second time, I roasted the tomatoes and seeded them. I doubled the amount of cumin and took a quarter of the salsa, pureed it and added it back. Then, I let it percolate in the fridge for a day and the flavor really spiked. I used hothouse tomatoes, which is not ideal, but in December, that's all the grocers had, so I lived with it. It was MUCH tastier in the second iteration after a night in the fridge and I think it earned another star.",
            "datePublished": "2023-12-03T19:35:37.670Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "whatsfordinner"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Great salsa recipe!! This was my first time making salsa and it was worth the effort! Only modifications made were to add a little more salt and cumin, and I also added a little chili power. We pulsed it in the food processor to give it a slightly finer consistency (so it’s less like a pico de gallo) and it was absolutely delicious! Tasted very similar to the salsa at our favorite Mexican restaurant. Next time I may add a little fresh garlic. Thanks for sharing; this recipe is a keeper!!",
            "datePublished": "2025-07-04T14:29:51.692Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Patricia Baughman"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I added a bit of sugar to this salsa, maybe about a half teaspoon and squeezed in a little more lime juice than the recipe called for. It was delicious.",
